{"id":"h285","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-physics","question":"AFabry-Perot etalon is adjusted so that for a wavelength of 5461A°, interference fringes are observed in a tele-scope focused for infinity. The etalon, of thickness 1.01 cm, is enclosed in a box with transparent windows from which the air can be exhausted. It is found that there is a shift of one fringe when the pressure is changed by 6.46 cm Hg. Find the index of refraction of the air at room temperature and at the original pressure, which was 77 cm Hg.\nIs the correct answer \"0.99789\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The correct answer is NO; the index of air is about 1.00032, not 0.99789.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"For an etalon, the optical path through the air gap is 2nt, and a one-fringe shift means 2tΔn = λ.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Δn for one fringe is λ/(2t), approximately 2.70 × 10⁻⁵.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The 6.46 cm Hg pressure change gives Δn per cm Hg of about 4.19 × 10⁻⁶.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Air's (n − 1) is proportional to pressure because index change follows density.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.4,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"At 77 cm Hg, n − 1 is about 3.22 × 10⁻⁴, so n ≈ 1.000322.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The result 1.0003 matches the known refractive index of air at atmospheric pressure.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"An index below 1 is unphysical for air at this pressure.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.9,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The value 0.99789 deviates from 1 by about 2 × 10⁻³, roughly seven times the known deviation, so it cannot follow from the measurements.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.3352,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":8,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":6,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":8,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":6,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":4,"j":8,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":5,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":5,"j":8,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"}],"readout_weights":[0.1667,0.0833,0.0833,0.0833,0.0667,0.1333,0.1,0.15,0.1333],"stages":[{"stage":"encode","qubits":[{"amp":0.9969,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0015,"bloch":[-0.9969,-0.0,0.0785],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9724,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0138,"bloch":[-0.9724,-0.0,0.2334],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9724,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0138,"bloch":[-0.9724,-0.0,0.2334],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9724,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0138,"bloch":[-0.9724,-0.0,0.2334],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9877,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0062,"bloch":[-0.9877,-0.0,0.1564],"purity":1.0},{"amp":0.9724,"phase":-3.1416,"p_yes":0.0138,"bloch":[-0.9724,-0.0,0.2334],"puri